diff --git a/docs/storage-accounting.md b/docs/storage-accounting.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d803c07
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/storage-accounting.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Storage accounting
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` read stored totals. They return zero
+until the first background calculation. The recurring `reconcile_storage` task
+discovers work every minute; totals are eventually consistent with attachment
+changes, subject to queue latency.
+
+Counted storage is the blob's `byte_size` for each card `image` attachment and each
+Action Text `embeds` attachment in board `public_description`, card `description`,
+and comment `body`. Shared blobs count once per attachment reference, so account
+usage is the sum of its boards' usage. Avatars, variants/previews, unattached
+uploads, remote URLs, and import/export archives do not count.
+
+## How it works
+
+* Attachment creation, destruction, purge, and detach write an attachment ID to
+  `storage_changes` in the source transaction. Card moves write a card ID. No
+  account-wide lock or attachment scan is required in these request callbacks.
+* `Storage::ReconcileJob` processes at most 500 notifications per transaction. It
+  reads current attachment ownership and sizes, compares them with
+  `storage_entries`, and applies only the differences to `storage_totals`.
+* An account's total row serializes its workers. Board/account adjustments,
+  ledger changes, and notification deletion commit together. Duplicate jobs,
+  repeated notifications, and retries cannot double-count. Notifications arriving
+  during processing remain queued for a subsequent batch.
+* Card moves transfer indexed ledger entries with SQL aggregates and updates;
+  they do not instantiate every attachment or comment on the card.
+* Existing attachments are automatically backfilled using an indexed UUID cursor,
+  in the same bounded batches. The cursor is committed with the accounting work,
+  so interrupted backfills resume safely. Once complete, normal processing never
+  rescans the account or board. No file contents are downloaded.
+
+The recurring task also recovers work if an enqueue fails or a worker stops.
+Imports call `account.reconcile_storage_later` to restart the background backfill,
+since imported IDs may precede the saved cursor and bulk inserts skip callbacks.
+This method is also safe to call manually for existing attachments. Other code
+that bulk-inserts attachments must call it too. Arbitrary SQL deletions/updates
+that bypass the normal attachment and card APIs are not tracked.
+
+Both SQLite and MySQL schemas are maintained; the new tables use UUID IDs and
+64-bit byte totals. Storage accounting tables are derived data, not part of the
+account export format.
